        "title": "Add CrossModel provider",
        "body": "## Summary\nAdds CrossModel as a disabled-by-default API-key provider for wallet balance and UTC daily, weekly, and monthly spend tracking.\n\n- Uses the documented CrossModel read-only API shape: `/v1/credits` for wallet balance and optional `/v1/usage` enrichment for usage windows.\n- Preserves currency end-to-end: JSON fields are `balance`, `uncollected`, and window `cost`, display uses the returned currency, and usage windows are omitted when `/credits` and `/usage` disagree on currency.\n- Keeps optional usage bounded and cancellation-safe; disabling optional usage fetches balance only and skips `/usage` entirely.\n- Rejects unsafe endpoint overrides and cross-origin redirects while accepting same-origin redirects with default HTTPS/HTTP ports normalized.\n- Renders CrossModel balance and spend in menu/status snapshots, widget snapshots, JSON output, and default CLI text output.\n- Updates docs/provider count to 56 after Qoder plus CrossModel, and keeps the changelog entry in Unreleased. Thanks @hujuncheng!\n\n## Validation\n- `swift test --filter CrossModel`\n- `swift test --filter CLIOutputTests --filter CrossModel`\n- `swift test --filter ConfigurationDocsProviderIDTests`\n- `make check`\n- `make test`\n- Autoreview pass 1: `/tmp/codexbar-1747-autoreview-3.txt` clean, no actionable findings\n- Autoreview pass 2: `/tmp/codexbar-1747-autoreview-4.txt` clean, no actionable findings\n- `./Scripts/package_app.sh`\n- `CodexBar.app/Contents/Info.plist` `CodexGitCommit == e33983d58`\n- `codesign --verify --strict --deep --verbose=2 CodexBar.app`\n\n## Maintainer Proof\nMaintainer validation used parser/unit tests, synthetic endpoint fixtures, cancellation/redirect tests, and a production invalid-key probe only. I did not run an authenticated CrossModel balance probe.\n\nInvalid-key proof from the freshly packaged app:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"error\": {\n      \"code\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"provider\",\n      \"message\": \"Invalid CrossModel API 